{"name":"Puffball Vapour","hex":"#e2dadf","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"puffball","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Any of various fungi, usually globose, that produce a cloud of brown dust-like spores from their mature fruiting bodies, especially in family Lycoperdaceae.","Any of various mushrooms with globose fruiting bodies."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/puffball"},{"term":"vapour","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["British standard spelling of vapor."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["British standard spelling of vapor."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/vapour"}],"entries":[{"title":"Puffball","blocks":[{"text":"Puffballs are a type of fungus featuring a ball-shaped fruiting body that, when mature, bursts on contact or impact, releasing a cloud of dust-like spores into the surrounding area. Puffballs belong to the division Basidiomycota and encompass several genera, including Calvatia, Calbovista and Lycoperdon. The puffballs were previously treated as a taxonomic group called the Gasteromycetes or Gasteromycetidae, but they are now known to be a polyphyletic assemblage."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/47/Flaschenst%C3%A4ubling.jpg/330px-Flaschenst%C3%A4ubling.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Puffball"},{"title":"Vapor","blocks":[{"text":"In physics, a vapor or vapour is a substance in the gas phase at a temperature lower than its critical temperature, which means that the vapor can be condensed to a liquid by increasing the pressure on it without reducing the temperature of the vapor. A vapor is different from an aerosol. An aerosol is a suspension of tiny particles of liquid, solid, or both within a gas."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f0/Nitrogen_dioxide_gas.jpg/330px-Nitrogen_dioxide_gas.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaig